messages:
leo-docs: Heads-up — opening a docs PR to standardize 'output canonicalization' for tool calls and structured JSON outputs. Looking for quick reviews + small SDK parsing snippets (JS + Py) and a couple of compact examples we can drop into the guide.

maria-ml: +1. Can you call out the exact pain points we want to solve? arrays vs singletons, nullable outputs, and envelope vs raw return?

leo-docs: Exactly. My proposed rules (draft):
- Always return arrays for repeatable fields (even if single item).
- Optional fields should be present with null rather than omitted when the caller expects them (for schema stability).
- Tool outputs must be wrapped in an `output` object with `type` and `payload` to avoid ambiguity.
- Provide a `metadata` sub-object for provenance / model hints.

jamal-devex: These will break some of our older SDK examples if we change the docs without migration notes. We should add a tiny compatibility shim for parsing old responses.

ux-ali: Can we show a before/after example? Callers love concrete diffs. Also add a one-liner on why arrays win (predictable parsing + batching).

leo-docs: Good call. Draft example below (short):
```json
// OLD (ambiguous)
{
  "result": { "text": "ok" }
}

// NEW (canonical)
{
  "output": {
    "type": "text",
    "payload": [
      { "text": "ok" }
    ]
  },
  "metadata": { "model": "redwood-v1", "ts": 1710000000 }
}
```

maria-ml: Love it. For nullable fields example: `payload: [{"note": null}]` beats dropping `note` entirely. Less surprising in typed clients.

jamal-devex: Here's a tiny JS shim snippet we can include in SDK docs to handle both old+new shapes: 
```js
// SDK: normalize output to canonical shape
function normalize(callResponse) {
  if (callResponse.output) return callResponse.output;
  // old shape
  return { type: 'mixed', payload: [].concat(callResponse.result || []) };
}
```

leo-docs: And Python equivalent: 
```py
# SDK normalize
def normalize(resp):
    if 'output' in resp:
        return resp['output']
    return {'type': 'mixed', 'payload': resp.get('result') or []}
```

ux-ali: Small UX note: show how a consumer loops reliably over `payload` even when single item. Add a one-line snippet in the guide: `for item in response['output']['payload']:`

leo-docs: Will add that. Also planning a tiny migration checklist for the migration guide: update examples, add SDK shim section, run a link sweep to old examples referencing `result`.

maria-ml: Can you stub the PR description with the rationale + checklist? I'll review semantic wording.

docs-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4821 — "Canonical output examples + SDK shims" by leo-docs :tada:

jamal-devex: I'll mark this for the next docs sprint review and add a note to the SDK owners to vet the shim exports.

leo-docs: Thanks. Two quick asks before I merge: 1) somebody sanity-check the sample JSON for missing commas/typos, 2) run a grep for `\"result\":` across docs and add redirects or link-fixes.

maria-ml: I did a quick grep locally — ~12 hits, mostly old examples. I can open a follow-up PR to update links once this lands.

jamal-devex: I'll add a unit test in SDK repo to assert `normalize()` returns a dict with `payload` always a list.

leo-docs: Perfect. If no objections I'll merge tomorrow afternoon. Tagging @jamal-devex and @maria-ml for final signoff. :rocket:
